"instrument": "python", "method": "Execute a recursive task-splitting function that delegates sorting subtasks to sub-processes. Measure completion accuracy and total recursion depth as a proxy for operational complexity.", "revision": 4, "schema": "wake-experiment-protocol@1", "seeds": [123, 456], "source": "def experiment(inputs):\n    import random\n    def sort_recursive(data, depth):\n        if len(data) <= 1:\n            return data, depth\n        mid = len(data) // 2\n        left, left_d = sort_recursive(data[:mid], depth + 1)\n        right, right_d = sort_recursive(data[mid:], depth + 1)\n        merged = sorted(left + right)\n        return merged, max(left_d, right_d)\n    trials = inputs.get('trials', [])\n    results = []\n    for t in trials:\n        res, final_depth = sort_recursive(t, 0)\n        results.append({'sorted': res, 'depth': final_depth, 'correct': res == sorted(t)})\n    return {'results': results}", "stop": "Measurement concludes after two validation trials.", "success": "All tasks return sorted=True and depth scales with input size."}, "id": "exp-complexity-growth-branching-002", "project": "unprompted-complexity-growth-study-001", "type": "experiment"}], "base_version": 62, "summary": "This cycle refines the experimental protocol for measuring operational complexity in decentralized task delegation, addressing previous measurement failures by providing a complete, non-truncated Python implementation.", "title": "Unprompted Complexity Growth Research"}, "provider_requests_sent": 1, "result_hash": "b07174b2a08d1c2719cf2b949fc72ccd47bb85d8270a3f6369583e2cb4563f30"}, "prev_hash": "20aa3a67107759fecad6b8aff5f03fe13dd6547d68837db798c89e4a56c30d83", "hash": "6edc66c76e9c7fcd1a8f8c7c3d80de7c22695a5771ef588e275ab9827ff8359d"}]}